the images of protesters lounging in the  pool cooking in the kitchen  and making themselves at home in the  presidential palace mark the  unforgettable and humiliating end to  gotabaya rajapaksa's short-lived tenure  as sri lankan president  elected in november 2019 he quickly  governed the country into a state of  destitution and desperation  by the time protesters forced him to  resign the nation had plummeted into an  economic crisis with no easy solutions  in sight  we have told the most powerful president  in the world to go home we have come  here braving tear gas water cannons and  bloodshed the protesters have already  released a list of demands they are not  requests these are the people's demands  it was a stunning reversal of fortunes  for rajapaksa and his powerful political  family  he was a third generation politician  his father was a member of parliament  and a cabinet minister his brother  served two terms as president  two other brothers also served in the  government  rajapaksa's supporters credited him with  helping to end a 26-year civil war  between the majority sinali's dominated  government and the minority tamil tigers  who wanted an independent state  an estimated 100 thousand people were  killed rajapaksa rose through the  military ranks and served during the  beginning of the war  then he emigrated to the united states  and worked as an i.t specialist and  manager of a convenience store  but in 2005 he returned to his homeland  to ensure his brother mahinda won a bid  to become president  rajapaksa became the defense minister  and his goal was to end the civil war  in 2006 he survived a suicide attack by  the tamil tigers  the u.n accused both sides of committing  war crimes  human rights groups accused rajapaksa of  disappearing opposition activists and  journalists and in 2015 interpol accused  him of engaging in corrupt practices to  obtain military hardware  he denied all the allegations  but what rajapaksa cannot deny is his  economic policies and allegations of  corruption led to dire shortages of food  fuel and medicine  whatever goodwill the island nation of  22 million once had for him and the  rajapaksa dynasty is now long gone  natasha name al jazeera
 

